course: dictionary
lesson: 10790
title: The word van
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A van is a vehicle that is bigger than a car and smaller than a truck. You can work out what a van is for by reading the words around it. «A delivery van brought the parcels to our door.» Parcels are carried, and a delivery van brings things to people, so a van carries goods.
explain: Look for clues about size and job. «The moving van was full of furniture for the new home.» Furniture such as sofas and beds is big, so a van must be large enough to carry it. Ask yourself what the word van is doing in the sentence, and whether your meaning still makes sense when you put it in.
explain: The plural of van is vans. «Two parked vans blocked the road.» There are two vans, so the s at the end means more than one. Some vans have seats for people, like a school team's van, and some have no back seats for carrying boxes or tools.
fact: A van is a vehicle bigger than a car and smaller than a truck.
fact: «Van» is a noun, and its plural is «vans».
fact: Some vans have seats for people, and some have no back seats, for carrying boxes, tools or furniture.
fact: Phrases with van include «a delivery van», «a camper van», «a moving van» and «by van».
fact: «In the van» can mean at the front of a march or a change, but this use is rare.
exercise: «A delivery van brought the parcels to our door.» What is a delivery van for? | *Carrying parcels and goods | Carrying water to the garden | Carrying people to the sea | Carrying a school team to a match
exercise: «Two parked vans blocked the road.» What does the s at the end of vans show? | It shows the vans belong to someone | It shows the vans are in the past | *It shows there is more than one | It shows the vans are asking a question
exercise: «The ice-cream van played music as it came down our street.» What kind of van is this? | A camper van for holidays | *An ice-cream van | A van for a school team | A moving van for furniture
test: «The camper van was parked by the lake for our summer holiday.» What is a camper van used for? | Delivering parcels | Carrying boxes of tools | *Going on holiday | Carrying furniture
test: «The moving van carried the sofa to the new home.» Where did the sofa go? | Up a hill | Into the sea | Back to the shop | *To a new home
exam: Which phrase names a van that carries furniture to a new home? | a camper van | by van | a delivery van | *a moving van
